## Prerequisites

- Git and Docker Engine with Compose v2 for the complete workflow.
{% if profile != 'frontend' %}- Python `>=3.11` and uv for backend development.
{% endif %}{% if profile != 'backend' %}- Node.js LTS `>=22.13 <23 || >=24 <25` and npm for frontend development.
{% endif %}

Backend containers use Python 3.13 by default. Frontend containers and generated CI use Node 24.
Project Forge tests Python 3.11 through 3.14 and the supported Node 22 and Node 24 LTS lines. The
Node 22 type definitions deliberately keep application code on the oldest supported API surface.
Odd-numbered releases and new even-numbered releases that have not reached LTS are outside the
support contract.

Check the profile-aware toolchain after committing the generated baseline:

```bash
project-forge doctor .
project-forge doctor . --require-docker
```

## First run with development Compose

The development stack starts only the selected components and applies pending migrations before the
API becomes ready.
{% if profile == 'frontend' and sample %}
The sample frontend expects an API reachable from Docker at
`http://host.docker.internal:8000`. Override `FRONTEND_API_PROXY_TARGET` when needed.
{% endif %}

```bash
cp .env.dev.example .env.dev
docker compose --env-file .env.dev -f docker-compose.dev.yml up --build
```

Active example values bind every host port to `127.0.0.1`. For a LAN demonstration, use only the
commented frontend overrides, replace the documentation address `172.20.0.10`, and add that exact
browser origin to `DEV_APP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`. Production `.env` and development `DEV_*` values are
deliberately isolated.

{% if profile != 'backend' %}- frontend: [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173)
{% endif %}{% if profile != 'frontend' %}- API docs: [http://localhost:8000/docs](http://localhost:8000/docs)
- readiness: [http://localhost:8000/health/ready](http://localhost:8000/health/ready)
{% endif %}

Stop the stack while preserving development volumes:

```bash
docker compose --env-file .env.dev -f docker-compose.dev.yml down
```

## Run local processes

Use component environment files for processes running directly on the host. The root `.env` is
reserved for production Compose.

{% if profile != 'frontend' %}### Backend

Start PostgreSQL{% if evented %} and Redis{% endif %}:

```bash
docker compose --env-file .env.dev -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d db{% if evented %} redis{% endif %}
```

In a backend terminal:

```bash
cp backend/.env.example backend/.env
cd backend
uv sync --frozen --all-groups{% if auth %} --extra auth{% endif %}{% if evented %} --extra evented{% endif %}
uv run app migrate status
uv run app migrate up
uv run app config check --json
uv run fastapi dev
```

The API refuses startup and readiness when migrations are pending.
{% if auth %}
Authentication maintenance:

```bash
cd backend
uv run app auth purge-expired --dry-run
uv run app auth purge-expired
```
{% endif %}{% if evented %}
Run the outbox relay in another backend terminal:

```bash
cd backend
uv run python -m app.events.worker
uv run app events status --json
uv run app events retry-failed --limit 100 --dry-run
```

The relay reclaims stale Redis pending messages and parks PostgreSQL outbox rows after the bounded
attempt limit. Inspect status before replaying; only explicitly retry parked rows after fixing the
underlying failure.
{% endif %}{% endif %}

{% if profile != 'backend' %}### Frontend

In a frontend terminal:

```bash
cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
cd frontend
npm ci
npm run dev
```

`VITE_API_BASE_URL` is empty by default so browser requests remain same-origin; a cross-origin value
is rejected at startup. `VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET` controls the server-side local Vite proxy.
PrimeVue uses Aura by default. The header theme control persists system, light, or dark mode in the
browser and keeps PrimeVue components synchronized with the application shell.
{% endif %}

